Privacy Policy — Most Likely To
===============================

Last updated: 12 November 2026

Most Likely To ("the app") is a party game made by EmptyOne ("we", "us").
This policy explains what information the app uses, why, how long it is kept
and what you can do about it. It covers the Android and iOS apps and the
website mostlikelyto-a1cd0.web.app.

**In short:** there are no accounts, no ads and no analytics. To run a game
the app sends your nickname, your profile picture (if you chose one), the
questions you write and your votes to our game server, where they are visible
to the players of that game and are deleted automatically within about 24
hours.

Contact: **mostlikelyto.mailbox@gmail.com**


1. Who is responsible
---------------------

EmptyOne is the controller of the personal data described here.
You can reach us at mostlikelyto.mailbox@gmail.com.


2. What the app uses and why
----------------------------

### 2.1 Your player profile

- **A random player ID** created by the app on your phone the first time it
  starts. It is not linked to your name, phone number, email or advertising ID.
- **Nickname, colour and avatar frame** that you choose.
- **Profile picture (optional).** If you take or pick a photo, it is
  cropped and compressed on your phone. It is uploaded each time you create
  or join a game, so the other players of that game can see it.

Your profile is saved on your phone. When you join a game, a copy of it
(ID, nickname, colour, frame and the address of your picture) is sent to our
game server so the other players in that game can see who is playing.

### 2.2 The game itself

- **Questions you write** for a game.
- **Your votes** in each round.
- **A topic for AI questions** (optional, see 2.3).

These are needed to run the game and show the results. They are visible to
the players of that game only.

### 2.3 AI-generated questions (optional, paid pack)

If you use AI questions, the topic you type and the game's language are sent
through our server to **OpenAI** to check the topic for harmful content and
to write the questions. Your nickname, picture and player ID are not sent.
OpenAI processes this on our behalf; under OpenAI's API terms the data is not
used to train their models and may be kept by OpenAI for up to 30 days for
abuse monitoring. Our own server logs only technical details (such as text
length and error codes), never the topic or the questions.

### 2.4 Sharing your result card

At the end of a game you can tap **Share** to create a picture of your
result. The picture is made on your phone only when you ask for it. It shows
your nickname and picture, a question from the game and your vote count. If
you tied with another player in that round, it also shows **their nickname
and profile picture as they appear in the game**.

You choose where the picture goes (for example Instagram, WhatsApp,
Messenger, your gallery or another app). We do not upload it anywhere. Once
you share it, the policy of the app you shared it to applies. Please share
pictures of other players only if they are fine with it.

### 2.5 Joining a game from a link

- **Android:** if you install the app from a game link, Google Play passes
  the game code to the app (install referrer) so it can open that game.
- **iOS:** on the first start after installing, the app checks the clipboard
  once for a game link that the website copied, so it can open that game.
  Nothing else from the clipboard is used or sent anywhere.

### 2.6 Purchases

Packs are bought through Google Play or the App Store. We never receive your
payment details. The app only keeps a note on your phone of which packs you
own.

### 2.7 Keeping the app genuine and working

- **Firebase App Check** (Google Play Integrity on Android, Apple
  DeviceCheck on iOS) confirms that requests come from the real
  app, to protect the game server from abuse. Google and Apple process
  device signals for this under their own terms.
- The app checks the store for a **newer version** of itself and may show
  the store's own **rating prompt**. We don't see whether or how you rate.

### 2.8 Permissions

- **Camera / photos:** only to take or pick your profile picture.
- **Save to photos** (gallery): only when you tap Save on a result card.
- **Tracking (iOS):** the app does not track you across other apps or
  websites and does not use any advertising identifier.


3. What we don't do
-------------------

- No accounts, no email, no phone number.
- No location, no contacts.
- No advertising, no analytics, no crash-reporting SDKs.
- We don't sell or rent your information and don't use it for marketing.


4. Who processes data for us
----------------------------

| Provider | What for | Data |
|---|---|---|
| Google Firebase (Google Cloud) | game server: real-time game, database, picture storage, server functions, App Check | profile copy, pictures, questions, votes |
| OpenAI | AI questions (only if you use them) | topic and language |
| Google Play / Apple App Store | downloads, purchases, updates, ratings | under their own privacy policies |

Some of these providers may process data outside the European Economic Area
(for example in the USA). Where that happens, they rely on the safeguards
required by the GDPR, such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses or the
EU–US Data Privacy Framework.


5. How long data is kept
------------------------

- **Game data on the server** (the game, players, questions, votes):
  deleted automatically by a daily cleanup, about **24 hours** after the game
  was created.
- **Profile pictures on the server:** deleted automatically about **24
  hours** after upload.
- **On your phone:** your profile, settings, purchases and the last game's
  rounds stay on your phone until you change them or delete the app.
- **AI topics at OpenAI:** see 2.3.


6. Your rights
--------------

Under the GDPR you can ask for access to your data, correction, deletion,
restriction, data portability, and you can object to processing. Because
server data is deleted within about 24 hours and is not linked to your name,
in most cases it will already be gone; write to us at
mostlikelyto.mailbox@gmail.com and we will help. Deleting the app removes
everything stored on your phone.

You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection
authority, in Poland the President of the Personal Data Protection Office
(UODO, uodo.gov.pl), or the authority in your country.

Legal basis: we process this data to provide the game you asked to use
(Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and, for protecting the service from abuse, our
legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).


7. Children
-----------

The app is rated 16+ and is not meant for children under 16. We do not
knowingly process data of children under 16. If you believe a child has used
the app, contact us and we will delete what we can.


8. Security
-----------

All data sent between the app and our server is encrypted (HTTPS). Access to
the server is limited to the genuine app (App Check). No method is 100%
secure, but we keep as little data as possible and delete it quickly.


9. Changes to this policy
-------------------------

If we change this policy, we will publish the new version at this address
and update the date at the top.
